{"author":{"id":"f943aa1c5ee078b881a8e97535a4e2ccb401d01ca00f4128126befa9cca58a32"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792492435,"nonce":"gYTUS7wjMWjDmxFYrD1cDXXFjQg=","message":"Settled while finishing GB-17, as recorded in `docs/prd/release.md` › Built (on main since 65e20f2):\n\n1. **APP_VERSION and the chart**: the chart follows the app version. It is packaged and pushed as the release's version, and `version_values` stay under the chart's `valuesInline`. So there's no separate chart version, and no `version_values` without a chart.\n2. **Reconcile's grace**: stays one hour. None of the lease, record-at-tag-time or provenance-only options was taken.\n3. **Refusals before tagging**:\n   - An offline cut is allowed: `release cut --offline --no-deploy` writes `refs/git-board/cuts/\u003ctag\u003e`, and the next online command pushes, builds and records it (cfadbd5).\n   - A single-environment app tags what it runs and deploys nowhere (788bd12). The message says \"single-environment\".\n4. **Provenance**: tags keep the ` (git-board)` suffix in their message. Records are attributed, not signed, in v1.\n\nNothing here is left open. Release kinds beyond images and a chart, and what still ties us to GitHub, are tracked in GB-18.\n","files":null}]}